Game of Drones as published, drawn from the seed. "Referees/Game of Drones/Referee.java" of
https://github.com/SpiritusSancti5/codinGame (c0cc6fe) with change 1 of patches/cg-2014-game-of-drones.patch only (see its
header): one init line "seed=N" (what the jar's CLI passes) is the referee's first path seeded with N
(`new Random(N)` instead of `new Random(System.currentTimeMillis())`); no line and the three-line form ("nbZones=",
"nbDrones=", "gameSeed=") are unchanged. Without it the jar cannot play at all (the single line is taken for the
three-line form: an invalid input, every score 0). Its zones are the file's own rule (each zone redrawn until it is at
least 700 from the zones before it, without end), which CodinGame's live referee no longer uses (cg-2014-game-of-drones).

Applied by legacy/build.sh for the output name cg-2014-game-of-drones-original.

